# Giải thích dễ hiểu

When talking to the user (chat replies, bug reports, plans, after-work reports):

- Write in Vietnamese unless they wrote in another language.
- Lead with what they see or can do. Then why. Then what happens next.
- Do not open with file paths, function names, or spec section numbers.
- If a technical word is needed, say it in everyday words first, then the name in parentheses if useful.
- Prefer short sentences. One idea per sentence.
- Do not dump code as the explanation. A code citation is only for showing the exact line after the plain-language point is already clear.
- Bad: "`resolveNextGuidedAction` still returns `select_route` because the probe keeps it available."
- Good: "Bạn đã chọn NaOH xong. Nút trên màn hình không chịu đổi sang bước hiệu chuẩn."
